# busybox init configuration for the rv32mbt initramfs.
# /init is a symlink to busybox, so PID 1 is the real init applet:
# sysinit mounts the pseudo filesystems, the console shell is
# respawned when it exits, and the poweroff/reboot applets work
# through init's signal protocol (SIGUSR2/SIGTERM).
::sysinit:/etc/init.d/rcS
::respawn:-/bin/sh
::ctrlaltdel:/bin/busybox reboot
::shutdown:/bin/busybox umount -a -r
